-- title:
--   Positive torus unit volume and finite twisted-centralizer unit volume
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra of degree $2$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, and let $v$ be a nonzero prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$ with completion $K_v$. Fix a unit $c \in K_v^{\times}$ and $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ such that the scalar matrix $c$, pushed into $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ along $a \mapsto 1 \otimes a$, is conjugate to the norm string $\prod_{i<[L:K]} \sigma^{i}(\delta)$ (entrywise action of $\sigma$ on the tensor factor), and such that no scalar matrix $z \in (L\otimes_K K_v)^{\times}$ satisfies $\mathrm{scalar}(z) = x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(x)$ for some $x$. Let $\tau'$ be a Haar measure for the Borel structure on the twisted centralizer $\{t : t\delta\sigma(t)^{-1} = \delta\}$, let $u_0$ lie in that group, and let $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ be such that $\mathrm{tr}(\gamma_0)^2 - 4\det(\gamma_0)$ is a unit and no conjugate $g^{-1}\gamma_0 g$ has both off-diagonal entries zero. Let $y_1$ satisfy $\gamma_0 = y_1^{-1}\,\bigl(\prod_{i<[L:K]}\sigma^{i}(u_0\delta)\bigr)\,y_1$ after transfer to $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$, and assume the intersection of the twisted centralizers of $\delta$ and of $u_0\delta$ is exactly the $y_1$-conjugate of the image of the centralizer of $\gamma_0$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$. Let $\tau_S$ and $\tau_T$ be Haar measures on that intersection and on the centralizer of $\gamma_0$, linked by the requirement that pushing $\tau_S$ forward along $s \mapsto y_1^{-1} s y_1$ agrees with pushing $\tau_T$ forward along the transfer map. Then, first, the real number obtained from the pushforward of $\tau_T$ to $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ of the set of $g$ in the centralizer of $\gamma_0$ with $|\det g| = 1$ and $|\mathrm{tr}\, g| \le 1$ is strictly positive; and second, $\tau'$ of the set of $t$ whose determinant equals $1 \otimes s$ for some $s \in K_v^{\times}$ with $|s| = 1$ is finite.
--
--   This is the volume-finiteness input for the elliptic twisted orbital comparison at a finite place: the unit group of the non-split torus attached to a regular elliptic $\gamma_0$ has positive finite Haar volume, while the set of elements of the twisted centralizer with determinant a unit coming from $K_v$ has finite Haar volume. It feeds the coupled elliptic transport and Weil-constant statement [`AutomorphicForm.exists_ellipticTransport_coupled_and_weilConst_mul_eq_of_not_isSigmaConjugate_scalar_of_finrank_eq_two`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_ellipticTransport_coupled_and_weilConst_mul_eq_of_not_isSigmaConjugate_scalar_of_finrank_eq_two).
